"""W8-E out-of-domain probe corpus (worker E, 2026-11-16).

All texts in this file were authored ORIGINALY for this probe by the
W8-E worker (an AI agent) as human-side probe inputs, EXCEPT the
``synthetic_template`` items, which are program-generated formulaic
prose (see the runner script). No text is copied from any published
source, and none comes from the six evaluation corpora
(RAID, MAGE, Beemo, DetectRL-X, GhostWriter, OpAI-Bench).

Coverage rationale (checked against the cached corpora on 2026-11-16):
RAID covers abstracts/books/news/poetry; DetectRL-X covers
News/Novel/SEO/Webtext/Wiki/Academic in ar/zh/en/fr/de/pt/ru/es;
GhostWriter covers student essays, Gutenberg, House of Commons,
CNN news, Bundestag (de), blogs, Euro court cases, arXiv;
Beemo covers QA/generation/rewrite/summarize; MAGE covers
cmv/eli5/tldr/xsum/wp/roct/hswag/yelp/squad/sci_gen; OpAI-Bench
covers abstracts/essays/news/reports. The slices below are outside
all of those: Italian and Japanese (no corpus covers it/ja),
source code, recipes, commercial contracts, live sports commentary,
transcribed spoken interviews, mathematical proofs, support-chat
logs, song lyrics, and Early Modern English pastiche. RAID does
cover poetry, so the lyrics slice is flagged as NEAR-domain, not
fully out-of-domain.

Every text is above the detector's 80-word minimum as counted by
plain whitespace splitting, so a verdict of ``abstain`` on a slice
cannot be explained away by the length gate alone (the detector's
own word_count is recorded per item in the run artifact).
"""

